* Commit
    saves snapshot of your changes ONLY ON YOUR LOCAL PC
    DOES NOT UPDATE GITHUB
    use this frequently while coding to SAVE PROGRESS LOCALLY w/o interrupting teammates

* Commit Amend
    overwrites VERY LAST LOCAL COMMIT instead of creating new save point
    use for minor errors like typo and want to clean up history

* Commit & push
    save locally and to github repo
    use when done with task and want code safely backed up in cloud 
    DO IF READY FOR OTHERS TO SEE

* Commit & sync
    saves locally, pulls down any new changes in github then pushes your changes up
    use when working closely on shared branch